figure/

# Development scratch, which is not part of the package. What is kept, as of
# the 2026-09-30 cleanup, is what something still rests on:
#
# - the records (`TASKS.md`, `SHIP.md`, and the notes package code or the tests
#   cite by filename);
# - the tools (`check.sh`, `benchmark.Rmd`, the timing and bit-exactness
#   benches, `justfile`);
# - every script behind a number the package ships or its code cites, and the
#   ones `CLAUDE.md` names as the pattern for a simulation script;
# - parked work, which is `_dev/did/` and the Gibbs-prior patch.
#
# Results (`.rds`) are not tracked. The one exception that matters,
# `vignettes/survival-results.rds`, lives outside `_dev/` and ships; the
# survival outputs it is built from stay on disk. Scripts removed in the cleanup
# are in the history before it. `_dev/Reproduce/` is Linero's JASA replication
# package -- seven third-party GPL-2 packages -- kept as a reference and not
# ours to redistribute, so it is never tracked.
#
# `_dev/did/` is the parked difference-in-differences work: four designs that
# were built, measured and not shipped, kept because the measurements are worth
# more than the code and will be wanted if the field settles. Note the ordering:
# `_dev/*` excludes the directory itself, so `!_dev/did/` has to re-include it
# before any file inside can be un-ignored, and `_dev/did/*` then drops the
# `.rds` outputs.
_dev/*
!_dev/did/
_dev/did/*
